{
 "about": "Spot-effect sheet for Episode 1, keyed to EDL shot ids (the director's cut/edl*.json), read by sound/fx/fx.mjs (called by sound/mix.mjs). An event plays sound `sound` (a recipe in fx/synth.mjs, all synthesised: no recordings) at the start of shot `shot` + `at` seconds; an event whose shot is not in the cut is skipped. `gain_db`: peak level of the event before the master gain (dialogue stem is -17 LUFS integrated); `gain_to_db` ramps it over repeats. `pan` -1..1 (`pan_to`: across repeats, or across the sound if single). `repeat`: {n, every_s, jitter_s, vary_db, alt: [params per step]}. `seed`: variation (same seed = same sound). `duck_db` (default 3): dip under speech windows. `defaults.stem_gain_db`: added to every event (the one knob to set the whole fx level by ear). `space`: reverb (default from `space_of_set`). Spotting follows shotlist.json `sound` notes; nothing at 1A-15 ('Whisper close on mic; nothing else') or 1A-25 ('All sound pulls back to room tone').",
